  "details": "I'm working on a map that uses fog to cover up things in the distance, and so when past the fog it would be nice to have an LOD for that object. It's basically free optimization. \n\nThe problem is I could fine tune it perfectly in unity, but because the VRChat client has an LOD setting that further affects it, items will always be able to cull or go to a lower detail way sooner than I design the map to.\n\nAlternatively, I can design the map to work perfectly at the \"Low\" setting for VRChat, but then players who have their settings at high will have a worse performance even though they see exactly the same thing other players see.\n\nIn many cases that I've tried using LODs, it's ended up easier to forego them entirely due to the LOD settings players have without realizing. Though for now I'm designing LODs exclusively with the \"low\" settings in mind.",
